Bugfix: Raise the border contrast of fields and controls

Input fields, text areas, buttons and select boxes had no discernible
boundary. The border that separated them from the page carried 1.36:1, and
its button variant 1.32:1, where the standard asks for 3:1. Because the
inside of a field and the page behind it are both white, and a button fill
differs from the page by 1.12:1, that border was the only separation there
was.

They now draw it in a grey that reaches 4.05:1 against the page and keeps
reserve against the button fill and the grey surfaces. Fill colours, text
colours, corner radius and metrics are unchanged. The container of the
picker in the external storage settings, which shared the same border, was
raised with it.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 1.4.11
